## Plateau WHY (first attempt below the number-family averages — T45 88.2 · T53 85.6)
The stuck lens is **timing (76)**, as predicted in Plan — but the mechanism is sharper than predicted: it is a structural tension inside the two-act form itself. Act 1's measured anchors consume ~10 s of the 14 s segment window (scene lead → border ~4 s → settled 5–10 s → clear + HUD restore ~11 s); Act 2, whose schedule is allocation, then has only the remainder, and the lenses price BOTH sides of the squeeze: timing wants Act 1's settled card preserved through ~10 s with a visible scene-restoration beat before Act 2, while readability wants Act 2's settled hold extended to ~6 s. Both cannot fit a 14 s loop at the measured Act-1 anchors — the attempt chose Act-1 anchor fidelity (timing 58→76, motion 62→84 after the cures) and Act 2 paid for it (3.5 s settled). The interim wave's convergent HUD bug (three lenses) is fully cured and no longer costs anything. What was proven this attempt: the Act-1 card is MEASURED (form, text, standing window, HUD coupling, clear) — stronger than the Plan's allocation fallback; the chart draws on with value-derived geometry (purity 90); the remaining gap is the two-act time budget plus override-depth machinery, not the data-beat mechanic.

## Priced cures for the next attempt (practice job) — convergent first
1. **CONVERGENT (timing −24 + readability −18): the two-act time budget** — resolve the squeeze explicitly: either lengthen the cycle beyond the 14 s segment form for Act 2's reading hold (~6 s settled) with the segment match preserved for Act 1 only, or compress Act 1's lead (the measured scene-only lead is 3.5 s of low information) and give Act 2 the recovered seconds; the choice must be priced against the two-act basis, not silently made. Includes timing's sub-cures: border-only interval ~1 s at ~4 s (currently 200 ms at 3.5–3.7 s), settled through ~10 s, clear + HUD-2037 restoration visible ~11 s BEFORE Act 2 enters.
2. **Motion (−16): HUD restore timing + beam draw** — restore the HUD year only once the card has fully cleared (currently flips at clear start, 9.5 s, while the card is still visible); reveal the beam's LENGTH progressively (currently opacity over full width); spread chart construction beyond 500 ms so each stage is perceptible (the numeral currently gets the final ~100 ms).
3. **Reusability (−20) + purity (−10, convergent machinery): override depth** — enforce validation before construction (PROBLEMS currently never stops rendering); explicit array-replacement semantics (arrays cannot shrink via override); normalize draw-on staggering to configured element counts (a 5th step's progress interval reverses and it stays invisible at p=1 — a real latent defect at stepCount 5); move drawChart's reveal thresholds into CONFIG; bind the page background `#0b1526` into the palette; define signed-percent direction (positive values currently hang downward too) and per-beat HUD evidence year.
4. **Readability (−18): secondary text** — status/place/source ink 11 px → toward 12–13 px and the HUD day line 9 px → toward 11 px (the carried fit-table HIT), checking wrapping and card-to-chart clearance at 360 px in a rendered frame.

## Limitations carried
PIXEL-UNVERIFIED (no exercisable browser binary in this seat): all lens verdicts are source/record-based; fit evidence is PIL font-metric measurement (DejaVu stand-ins for Georgia) + node-harness logic tests; the comparison page is the render surface. Schedule basis `two-act`: Act 1's form and standing window are OBSERVED from segment frames; Act 2's form is frame-evidenced (ev/t492) and its schedule is allocation. The unit row is a labeled allocation (countable form of "1 in 5"; the specimen card carries none). Dialogue-coupling (entrances bound to speech cues) is unproven by construction — the clock is the schedule; the motion lens prices it as a next-attempt cure.
Catalogue-fidelity observations (for style-library/digestion): (1) digest P4-T19 cites ev/t392.jpg as the ALREADY MEASURED card frame — the card is NOT at t392 (that frame is the pre-card projection scene); builder segment frames place the card at source ≈392.5–399.5 s (border ~393, settled 394–399, gone by 400). The citation is mistimed, the technique stands. (2) The measured card text is "AI research system: about 1 in 5 claims did not hold up / KOSMOS · ARXIV 2511.02824" (USA · 2025) — richer than the digest's gloss ("about 1 in 5 claims did not hold up"); the build carries the measured text.

